"wiringreportlayer.errorY1NotPoweredDueToTemp.aw" = "Your thermostat isn't getting power from your home's wiring. It will shut down soon and your home will lose heating. Select More Info to fix your wiring now with a short-term solution. Learn more about a long-term solution at";
"wiringreportlayer.errorY1NotPoweredDueToTemp.info.aw" = "To restore power to your thermostat, first turn off power at the circuit breaker. If you're not sure which switch controls the thermostat, you may need to turn off power to your entire home.\n\nNext, remove your thermostat from the wall. Disconnect all Y wires.\n\nThen, only if you have both an Rc and Rh wire connected, disconnect only the Rc wire.\n\nWrap any exposed wire ends separately in electrical tape and push them back toward the wall. Then reattach your thermostat to the wall and turn the power back on.\n\nIf you don't troubleshoot your thermostat's wiring, it will shut down, and your home will lose heating. Learn more about a long-term solution at";
"wiringreportlayer.errorY1NotPoweredDueToTemp.info.singlerwire.aw" = "To restore power to your thermostat, first turn off power at the circuit breaker. If you're not sure which switch controls the thermostat, you may need to turn off power to your entire home.\n\nNext, remove your thermostat from the wall. Disconnect all Y wires.\n\nWrap any exposed wire ends separately in electrical tape and push them back toward the wall. Then reattach your thermostat to the wall and turn the power back on.\n\nIf you don't troubleshoot your thermostat's wiring, it will shut down, and your home will lose heating. Learn more about a long-term solution at";
